</rect></g><g fill="var(--color-mono-400)"><rect x="524" y="24" width="34" class="svelte-cqh9tb"></rect><rect x="911" y="24" width="34" class="svelte-cqh9tb"></rect><rect x="730" y="24" width="42" class="svelte-cqh9tb"></rect></g><g fill="var(--color-mono-400)"><rect x="524" y="18" width="34" class="svelte-cqh9tb"></rect><rect x="911" y="18" width="34" class="svelte-cqh9tb"></rect><rect x="729" y="18" width="44" class="svelte-cqh9tb"></rect></g><g fill="var(--color-mono-400)"><rect x="524" y="12" width="34" class="svelte-cqh9tb"></rect><rect x="911" y="12" width="34" class="svelte-cqh9tb"></rect><rect x="730" y="12" width="42" class="svelte-cqh9tb"></rect></g><g fill="var(--color-mono-400)"><rect x="524" y="6" width="34" class="svelte-cqh9tb"></rect><rect x="911" y="6" width="34" class="svelte-cqh9tb"></rect><rect x="734" y="6" width="34" class="svelte-cqh9tb"></rect></g><g fill="var(--color-mono-400)"><rect x="524" width="34" class="svelte-cqh9tb"></rect><rect x="911" width="34" class="svelte-cqh9tb"></rect><rect x="745" width="12" class="svelte-cqh9tb"></rect></g></svg><!--]--></footer><!----></div> <!--[!--><!--]--><!----><!--]--> <!--[!--><!--]--><!--]-->
			
			<script>
				{
					__sveltekit_10y6csw = {
						base: new URL("..", location).pathname.slice(0, -1)
					};

					const element = document.currentScript.parentElement;

					Promise.all([
						import("../_app/immutable/entry/start.DQJu0JU4.js"),
						import("../_app/immutable/entry/app.CGavIq-3.js")
					]).then(([kit, app]) => {
						kit.start(app, element, {
							node_ids: [0, 2, 9],
							data: [{"type":"data","data":{draftMode:false},"uses":{}},null,{"type":"data","data":{post:{_type:"post",authors:[{name:"Poolside team",organization:null,role:null}],body:[{_key:"493d01caa5c3",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"a3b7d6863a72",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Today we’re releasing Laguna S 2.1, a significant step forward in our development of models that pursue longer horizon work and make effective use of reasoning."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"3af46eaf329b",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"b5a55255e061",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Laguna S 2.1 is a 118B total parameter Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) model with 8B activated parameters per token and supports a context window of up to 1M tokens in thinking and no-thinking modes. It went from the start of training to launch in under nine weeks, and on long-horizon coding benchmarks it holds its own against models many times its size. For every benchmark score we publish today, we are releasing full trajectories for every trial in the final evaluation set at "},{_key:"6f1acf6055c2",_type:"span",marks:["182878d95b98"],text:"trajectories.poolside.ai"},{_key:"18a03cd6b611",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"."}],markDefs:[{_key:"182878d95b98",_type:"link",href:"http://trajectories.poolside.ai/"}],style:"normal"},{_key:"396992ceac37",_ref:"17d06271-38e7-4fba-bf16-9e1831fe8a6a",_type:"chart",chartType:null,id:"laguna-s",markDefs:null,name:"Laguna S"},{_key:"6ab18d4be786",_type:"markdown",content:"\u003Ctable>\n\u003Cthead>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Cth>\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>\u003Cdiv style=\"min-width:90px;\">Laguna S 2.1 (118B-A8B)\u003C/div>\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Tencent Hy3 (295B-A21B)\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Inkling (975B-A41B)\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>\u003Cdiv style=\"min-width:130px;\">Nemotron 3 Ultra (550B-A55B)\u003C/div>\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>\u003Cdiv style=\"min-width:160px;\">DeepSeek-V4-Pro Max (1.6T-A49B)\u003C/div>\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Kimi K3 (2.8T-A50B)\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>\u003Cdiv style=\"min-width:90px;\">Qwen 3.7 Max (—)\u003C/div>\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>\u003Cdiv style=\"min-width:90px;\">Muse Spark 1.1 (—)\u003C/div>\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>\u003Cdiv style=\"min-width:90px;\">Claude Fable 5 (—)\u003C/div>\u003C/th>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/thead>\n\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Cdiv style=\"min-width:160px;\">Terminal-Bench 2.1\u003C/div>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>70.2\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>71.7\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>63.8\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>56.4\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>64.0\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>88.3\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>74.5\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>80\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>88.0\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>SWE-Bench Multilingual\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>78.5\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>75.8\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>67.7\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>76.2\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>78.3\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>SWE-Bench Pro (Public Dataset)\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>59.4\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>57.9\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>54.3\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>55.4\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>60.6\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>61.5\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>80.3\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>DeepSWE\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>40.4\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>9.0\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>69.0\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>53.3\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>70.0\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>SWE Atlas (Codebase QnA)\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>46.2\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>27.2\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>42.2\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>Toolathlon Verified\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>49.7\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>45.5\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>34.3\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>55.9\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>75.6\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>-\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\n",markDefs:null},{_key:"1cbbda4c3b7a",_type:"markdown",content:"\u003Cnav class=\"article-actions\" aria-label=\"Laguna S 2.1 links\">\n\t\u003Ca href=\"https://chat.poolside.ai \">Talk to the model (no sign-up needed)\u003C/a>\n\t\u003Ca href=\"https://huggingface.co/poolside/Laguna-S-2.1 \">Hugging Face\u003C/a>\n\t\u003Ca href=\"https://trajectories.poolside.ai \">Evaluation Trajectories\u003C/a>\n\u003C/nav>",markDefs:null},{_key:"96ea6c57c40e",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"c97a7029eae7",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Punching above its weight class"}],markDefs:[],style:"h2"},{_key:"45b2cd8d33b3",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"8bbfb8797590",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Laguna S 2.1 is, as far as we can measure, "},{_key:"a899cba1391a",_type:"span",marks:["strong"],text:"the most capable agentic coding model in its weight class by a wide margin"},{_key:"dd5761df5559",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"e08296e72bab",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"ea8091179746",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"S 2.1 scores 70.2% on Terminal-Bench 2.1 in our agent harness with thinking enabled. Its compact size makes it uniquely suitable for complex work on local machines."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"e0bd47c97212",_ref:"0c7d9f16-080f-4b68-acdc-7d893ca46966",_type:"articleModule",id:"laguna-s-2-1-terminal-leaderboard",kind:"editorialVisual",markDefs:null,name:"Laguna S 2.1 Terminal leaderboard",promptBlock:null},{_key:"519cbcf7fe9d",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"c5438e43e491",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Terminal-Bench 2.1 evaluates a wide, high-quality set of long-horizon tasks where an agent model is connected to its environment through a terminal. Laguna S 2.1 is a standout model in its size category on this benchmark."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"752f173b2b43",_ref:"613d4356-f358-491e-bb65-f19300f465d4",_type:"chart",chartType:"scatterPlot",id:"laguna-s-2-1-size-score",markDefs:null,name:"Laguna S 2.1 size versus score"},{_key:"f9c6134d7e84",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"b4f492f90994",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"A closer look at DeepSWE"}],markDefs:[],style:"h2"},{_key:"0c9a93947df2",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"a90eab9fce2c",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"The benchmarks above are all meaningful, and we're glad to be close to the frontier on them. But part of that closeness is a property of maturing benchmarks: as the frontier advances, top scores cluster in the 70-90% range and models that behave very differently end up no more than a few points apart. Datacurve’s DeepSWE still has significant headroom. Its tasks are longer-horizon and hard to partially solve, and the scores actually spread: frontier models range from 54% to 73% on the v1.1 variant, with some 1T+ parameter open models scoring below 10%."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"6190f3da37a0",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"1e25dff822af",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"On DeepSWE v1.1, Laguna S 2.1 scores "},{_key:"4bdf599a00cb",_type:"span",marks:["strong"],text:"40.4"},{_key:"4a6ea2bfe522",_type:"span",marks:[],text:" in thinking mode in pool harness."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"970c6075acf3",_ref:"7faddbb4-c643-4e51-9bc0-ab75a40d022e",_type:"articleModule",id:"laguna-s-2-1-deepswe-leaderboard",kind:"editorialVisual",markDefs:null,name:"Laguna S 2.1 DeepSWE leaderboard",promptBlock:null},{_key:"18e5b0df7b9b",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"fee32c24c715",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"It is worth noting that Laguna S 2.1 scored 40.4% in our agent harness, pool, not mini-swe-agent which DeepSWE’s leaderboard uses. For other models we report maximal over reported scores which for most models are the official leaderboard results reported by Datacurve. While this makes scores less comparable, we don’t believe it puts us in a particularly advantageous position as it’s been reported that many of the models score the same or better in mini-swe-agent compared to their native harnesses. Every trajectory in the final evaluation run is available "},{_key:"9bb0a41577bd",_type:"span",marks:["34398f19c59e"],text:"here"},{_key:"500049a412e3",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"."}],markDefs:[{_key:"34398f19c59e",_type:"link",href:"https://trajectories.poolside.ai/?benchmark=deep-swe&sort=result&dir=desc&variant=thinking"}],style:"normal"},{_key:"e0bb940b401f",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"41c1023656a0",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Evaluation methodology"}],markDefs:[],style:"h2"},{_key:"44c0a2a2b0fc",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"eb0928521837",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Evaluation of agent models is notoriously difficult due to prevalence of reward hacking. We have previously written about "},{_key:"2cc193c6bc3a",_type:"span",marks:["d5e0eb94723b"],text:"reward hacking"},{_key:"868b686fec41",_type:"span",marks:[],text:" in leading benchmarks and our evaluations system and rigor as part of the technical report on our Laguna M.1 and XS.2 models. Recent work has focused on adversarial judging to increase reward hacking detection."}],markDefs:[{_key:"d5e0eb94723b",_type:"link",href:"https://poolside.ai/blog/through-the-looking-glass"}],style:"normal"},{_key:"bec43a91913f",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"971b26030ffe",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"With this release, we are making all trajectories from our final evaluations of the published Laguna S 2.1 checkpoint available to view and download at "},{_key:"5cae440fee1f",_type:"span",marks:["8513fc087162"],text:"trajectories.poolside.ai"},{_key:"7ded98d393a8",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"."}],markDefs:[{_key:"8513fc087162",_type:"link",href:"http://trajectories.poolside.ai/"}],style:"normal"},{_key:"7619152c4d49",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"fe178fd6e21e",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Seeing the model work"}],markDefs:[],style:"h2"},{_key:"283b42a51536",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"265d3b942b1f",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Benchmark scores give a quantitative view into the model behavior, but to get a better intuitive understanding of how the model works it’s useful to look into runs on real world tasks. We share three such tasks with unedited trajectories and commentary."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"850638691873",_ref:"8cca33ab-66c3-4b1f-b998-de0ec497ef79",_type:"articleModule",id:"laguna-s-2-1-case-browser-engine",kind:"editorialVisual",markDefs:null,name:"Laguna S 2.1 Browser engine case study",promptBlock:null},{_key:"5970edc94eaa",_ref:"57cec7b1-1bec-40e4-a637-743b228fccda",_type:"articleModule",id:"laguna-s-2-1-case-harness-optimization",kind:"editorialVisual",markDefs:null,name:"Laguna S 2.1 Harness optimization case study",promptBlock:null},{_key:"0b085f32aab1",_ref:"ae7887c3-23e6-4005-ad3e-df05a3c57002",_type:"articleModule",id:"laguna-s-2-1-case-erdos-397",kind:"editorialVisual",markDefs:null,name:"Laguna S 2.1 Erdős problem 397 case study",promptBlock:null},{_key:"404f42c5bbbd",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"c9784a03edd4",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Thinking effort"}],markDefs:[],style:"h2"},{_key:"b0d97e57e96e",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"4ac6948b407e",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Laguna S 2.1 has two thinking modes: off and max (enabled by default) where it determines the right thinking/test-time compute budget for a given problem. We have observed coherent, productive thinking over several hours and hundreds of thousands of tokens in length."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"145ec082b75b",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"2563b378b0e3",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Max thinking lifts S 2.1’s score on Terminal-Bench 2.1 from 60.4% to 70.2% and on DeepSWE from 16.5% to 40.4%. We are releasing this model without user-configurable effort (low-medium-high) control today to get Laguna S 2.1 into the hands of users immediately."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"265217274ce5",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"52fef17a970c",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"The two modes still give you a real choice, and it's worth seeing what each point costs:"}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"832659a0d089",_ref:"7b19f024-6860-4ae5-a9dc-7731628074e0",_type:"articleModule",id:"laguna-s-2-1-efficiency-curve",kind:"editorialVisual",markDefs:null,name:"Laguna S 2.1 Thinking cost efficiency curve",promptBlock:null},{_key:"caae143d3269",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"37d9a6a10466",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Limitations"}],markDefs:[],style:"h2"},{_key:"dd5a48c417b5",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"00ff5f6c02ee",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"We are excited about the capabilities of Laguna S 2.1, in general as well as in the context of its size. In order to learn quickly we are making the model available with some known limitations that we are working on for the next iteration:"}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"944d27c86a96",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"423fac684a8e",_type:"span",marks:["strong"],text:"Harness overfitting"},{_key:"ab3125155966",_type:"span",marks:[],text:": in some cases, we observe that Laguna S 2.1 struggles with adhering to tool schema definitions in third-party agent harnesses (e.g., the terminal tool in Hermes Agent) which are very similar to those in our native harness but with slight differences. In this case, the model may rely on its memory of the tool interface on the first use of the tool instead of following the definition. This is typically resolved through in-context learning should the harness reject the invalid tool call and ask the model to retry."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"a304a8a30217",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"240e3aab47d3",_type:"span",marks:["strong"],text:"Nested tool calls"},{_key:"20b724c95d8c",_type:"span",marks:[],text:": Laguna S 2.1 is guided to use a tool call format where tool calls are marked by XML-like tags:"}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"6381765d9ba1",_type:"code",code:"\u003Ctool_call>terminal\u003Carg_key>cmd\u003C/arg_key>\u003Carg_value>uname -a\u003C/arg_value>\u003C/tool_call>",language:"xml",markDefs:null},{_key:"50510c896d69",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"2937ca4704bd",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"In cases where a tool argument expects a JSON array (e.g., Pi’s edit tool) the model may generate incorrectly escaped or invalid JSON."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"e9eaafc46638",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"93676d560027",_type:"span",marks:["strong"],text:"Longer than expected thinking duration/overthinking"},{_key:"963f83268748",_type:"span",marks:[],text:": Laguna S 2.1 may think for long sequences before making progress, especially when working through competition mathematics problems. In future models we will introduce effort control for thinking as well as seeking to improve thinking efficiency."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"5d022b4ecac8",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"c087a27fd27c",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"What actually changed in this model"}],markDefs:[],style:"h2"},{_key:"fa8f4c82efd3",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"aff48ab9338e",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"If the bet is long-horizon work, what did we improve that helps a model keep going? For S 2.1, it isn't just increasing the model size."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"f60a6f5483c6",_ref:"7e50b0c4-8135-4734-ad48-7ba13342047f",_type:"quote",author:{name:"Pengming Wang",organization:"Poolside",role:"Co-head of Applied Research"},markDefs:null,text:"What we've done in this model is not necessarily add more intelligence, but improve the behaviors that lead to a more capable model: more verification, less taking things for granted, not declaring victory early, and being more persistent."},{_key:"6acc86f7263e",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"73d3d7a684f7",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"The easiest way to see this is to watch the model work. Earlier Laguna series models would declare victory on a partially-passing test suite or abandon an approach two steps before it worked, S 2.1 keeps going."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"c381317dc163",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"d00b2ebe1905",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"We believe in scaling laws and will keep training larger models. What Laguna S 2.1 suggests is that raw intelligence is one axis, and the model's "},{_key:"5219cb6f67c1",_type:"span",marks:["em"],text:"way of working"},{_key:"2e4061e071ba",_type:"span",marks:[],text:" (persistence, verification, willingness to backtrack) is a second axis that matters immensely. We're investing in both: our next, larger, Laguna series model began pre-training last week."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"6e5ee5c478e6",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"d065c2347986",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"A strong base, then new post-training"}],markDefs:[],style:"h3"},{_key:"64c028d6f9e7",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"fdbf83e3c93a",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Laguna S 2.1 is a scale-up of the Laguna XS family, trained on exactly the same pre-training data as XS 2.1: the step from XS 2.1 to S 2.1 was scale, training-code fixes, and small recipe changes, not new data. S 2.1 is also our first model where RL was done in FP8 precision, accelerating that part of the training."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"b4e354f85b40",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"59e41953a09f",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"The long agentic sessions in this post routinely accumulate hundreds of thousands of tokens of working context. Extending to a 1M-token context window enables the strongest performance on hard tasks."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"10ac6b417565",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"45518a639eba",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"The majority of what separates S 2.1 from the XS models comes from post-training, in two stages: an SFT stage that bootstraps capabilities partly with synthetic data, then RL, reserved for tasks the model can't yet solve at a high pass rate."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"8fec76e6252c",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"e7c9ed99f9df",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Distribution of post-training tasks"}],markDefs:[],style:"h3"},{_key:"a705d201241d",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"0c9e659dd8e6",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Our training corpus spans 409k agentic and non-agentic environments; within this, 83k setups are dedicated to terminal use cases, while 168k target standard software engineering workflows. These task sets were curated from open-source repositories, synthesized by our internal teams, including a specialized system for automatic dependency installation, or secured via strategic acquisitions from external data vendors."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"d37c6a5f8cc3",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"13750b0f8a97",_type:"span",marks:["strong"],text:"Software-engineering tasks"},{_key:"70ac57730406",_type:"span",marks:[],text:" are mostly grounded in real code history: the largest source reproduces real commits (~38,000 tasks across ~17,000 repositories). The next reproduces merged pull requests and the remaining tasks are to fix injected bugs or reconstruct deleted files against a test suite. New for S 2.1 is agentic repository installation: given a repository, install every dependency and get the test suite running."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"f1b074461bb7",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"73758a4d61ef",_type:"span",marks:["strong"],text:"Terminal tasks"},{_key:"b391e59edfb3",_type:"span",marks:[],text:" come from datasets where agents build unseen environments and tasks from a seed."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"28e8ed62d04e",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"8f5fe003a392",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"What changed in the training loop"}],markDefs:[],style:"h3"},{_key:"ab506ed2fe71",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"a67e23d4e55b",_type:"span",marks:["strong"],text:"More generous rollout budgets"},{_key:"8cd7d9deeabd",_type:"span",marks:[],text:": substantially longer timeouts, more tokens per turn, and more turns per task than any model before it (likely one reason for its persistence)."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"f867624cb7fb",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"6e3a2b7d1a6c",_type:"span",marks:["strong"],text:"Better sandbox infrastructure"},{_key:"f3805c540ee5",_type:"span",marks:[],text:": RL moved to a new sandboxing service, enabling background processes, selective network blocking to shrink reward-hacking surface and artifact caching to avoid overloading external services."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"ddecf15949dc",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"9198b6a5cef9",_type:"span",marks:["strong"],text:"Multi-harness rollouts"},{_key:"7a14b1552005",_type:"span",marks:[],text:": the same prompts are rolled out in several agent harnesses, so the model learns behaviors that carry across scaffolds instead of overfitting to one."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"8aa349830a43",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"9177372b122a",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"The bets we're making"}],markDefs:[],style:"h2"},{_key:"7fcf4b301ed0",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"b4ef380bf8ec",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Laguna S 2.1 began pre-training on 4,096 NVIDIA H200 GPUs on May 22, 2026, 60 days ago. The Model Factory supports a high cadence of releases because building on foundations of work done, whether in pre-training data, architecture ablations or our evaluations stack, is automatic. In particular, advancements in post-training have enabled us to unlock more from test-time compute. Of all models we have trained to date, Laguna S 2.1 has the greatest delta in evaluations and perceived quality between its non-thinking mode and thinking mode: its internal monologue is very effective, especially for harder, complex problems."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"e64fb142a944",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"1774f8e0d134",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"A small team can only move this fast by focusing. We focus on two bets."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"ef45317c71c2",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"86acd8fec27d",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"The first bet: we continue to focus on agentic coding capabilities. The path to intelligence runs through coding capability and the flexible interface that is software. This is increasingly evident as model intelligence advances: we now see hours- and days-long coherent work from models acting as agents, using software to interact with their environment. Laguna S 2.1 shows capabilities in this domain that were reserved for frontier models just 6 months ago at a small enough size to run on a single "},{_key:"d2ab25088c94",_type:"span",marks:["fdd0a6265428"],text:"NVIDIA DGX Spark"},{_key:"24da05224ec2",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"."}],markDefs:[{_key:"fdd0a6265428",_type:"link",href:"https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/products/workstations/dgx-spark/",tab:true}],style:"normal"},{_key:"5d38027331d7",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"1ef786a27a16",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"The second bet is that the web can be decompressed: almost everything humanity has written records the answer, not the thinking that got there, and we believe reinforcement learning can recover that thinking. This release is evidence for the first bet. The second we're still actively developing and excited to share more about in the future."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"81d75f664b9d",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"024953027673",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Three models in three months"}],markDefs:[],style:"h2"},{_key:"79e7453b3fc7",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"ae5bac75e172",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Our internal platform for research and engineering, which we refer to as the Model Factory, allows us to industrialize the model development process. We invest heavily into continuously improving the process of how we conduct research and model building; to maximize research iteration and integration speed, and to minimize the amount of attention researchers need to pay to bookkeeping and infrastructure."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"53839a843241",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"56934e122acd",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"In less than 3 months from our Laguna M.1 release, we have pushed our techniques to deliver a substantially stronger model at half the running size. We are taking this forward to larger and larger models over the coming year."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"ee73c06a67e5",_ref:"6de1b197-8668-4b03-9497-e90fd1a28fee",_type:"articleModule",id:"laguna-s-2-1-release-timeline",kind:"timeline",markDefs:null,name:"Laguna S 2.1 Release timeline",promptBlock:null},{_key:"be120cedfffa",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"0f27fd39d1ee",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Get started"}],markDefs:[],style:"h2"},{_key:"0a0d7c6802dc",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"c3131c44011a",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"Laguna S 2.1 is available on "},{_key:"49b994bd13c7",_type:"span",marks:["059f24d01a7a"],text:"Hugging Face"},{_key:"59a5b7eb88da",_type:"span",marks:[],text:" from day one under OpenMDW-1.1, with BF16, FP8, INT4 and NVFP4 weights, official GGUF and MLX conversions, and official DFlash draft models."}],markDefs:[{_key:"059f24d01a7a",_type:"link",href:"https://huggingface.co/poolside/Laguna-S-2.1"}],style:"normal"},{_key:"60103ab8630f",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"c116f0edf7e1",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"We worked across the ecosystem so developers can run Laguna S 2.1 where they already build. "},{_key:"31cf4b16ef35",_type:"span",marks:["ce6200eba280"],text:"NVIDIA"},{_key:"c8284bfbe331",_type:"span",marks:[],text:" helped optimize inference across its hardware, from TRT-LLM serving and NVFP4 on Blackwell systems down to a single NVIDIA DGX Spark. "},{_key:"4e9f4aa89ffb",_type:"span",marks:["c1dac589a016"],text:"vLLM,"},{_key:"127924552d08",_type:"span",marks:[],text:" "},{_key:"70aa27de9d55",_type:"span",marks:["e6786957f38d"],text:"SGLang "},{_key:"2b8f1b70b0d8",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"and "},{_key:"ffa0a411418e",_type:"span",marks:["ef74a72bd492"],text:"Ollama"},{_key:"24a2e4ee8257",_type:"span",marks:[],text:" support open serving and local inference from day one."}],markDefs:[{_key:"ce6200eba280",_type:"link",href:"https://www.nvidia.com"},{_key:"c1dac589a016",_type:"link",href:"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm"},{_key:"e6786957f38d",_type:"link",href:"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang"},{_key:"ef74a72bd492",_type:"link",href:"https://ollama.com"}],style:"normal"},{_key:"d52fa5349794",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"f03c1451b080",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"For hosted access, Laguna S 2.1 is available through "},{_key:"4c52c76fbea8",_type:"span",marks:["807ad40cf7d7"],text:"Baseten’s Model Library"},{_key:"9614e844be33",_type:"span",marks:[],text:" and Frontier Gateway, "},{_key:"9a670a841aa9",_type:"span",marks:["58aa38c40f27"],text:"OpenRouter"},{_key:"f789dc5e071e",_type:"span",marks:[],text:", including a free endpoint and a dedicated 1M-context deployment, and "},{_key:"0cc665f6557d",_type:"span",marks:["c03f6ced8bd0"],text:"Vercel AI Gateway"},{_key:"eba41961a728",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"."}],markDefs:[{_key:"807ad40cf7d7",_type:"link",href:"https://www.baseten.co/library/laguna-s-21/"},{_key:"c03f6ced8bd0",_type:"link",href:"https://vercel.com/ai-gateway/models?q=laguna"},{_key:"58aa38c40f27",_type:"link",href:"https://openrouter.ai/poolside/laguna-s-2.1"}],style:"normal"},{_key:"f60bec76238c",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"b2e1e294817f",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"You can also use Laguna S 2.1 through "},{_key:"4bf15c8734c6",_type:"span",marks:["d169405de4b2"],text:"Kilo"},{_key:"7d709d5e1131",_type:"span",marks:[],text:", "},{_key:"b9fa3fbf079f",_type:"span",marks:["0de673591709"],text:"Hermes Agent"},{_key:"4d6f444d8ce2",_type:"span",marks:[],text:", "},{_key:"92890391e39d",_type:"span",marks:["8deae9cdef71"],text:"pi"},{_key:"5180317b892c",_type:"span",marks:[],text:", "},{_key:"24f4d9327901",_type:"span",marks:["8252a7c9da4c"],text:"OpenCode"},{_key:"5c481f26074b",_type:"span",marks:[],text:", "},{_key:"f91e5219da5e",_type:"span",marks:["0a0ea0fa6220"],text:"OpenClaw"},{_key:"fa23ca6521f5",_type:"span",marks:[],text:" and "},{_key:"5ad4b0021c37",_type:"span",marks:["b0fd7c52b22f"],text:"Cline"},{_key:"5f8a12d6929a",_type:"span",marks:[],text:", as well as "},{_key:"f977c7ad1216",_type:"span",marks:["bc8a1240ef4c"],text:"pool"},{_key:"86bfa6f0eaf4",_type:"span",marks:[],text:", our terminal-based coding agent. In pool, toggle thinking per session with "},{_key:"e10a396c2eee",_type:"span",marks:["code"],text:"/thought-level"},{_key:"0309062e9b42",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"."}],markDefs:[{_key:"0de673591709",_type:"link",href:"https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"},{_key:"8deae9cdef71",_type:"link",href:"https://pi.dev/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"},{_key:"8252a7c9da4c",_type:"link",href:"https://opencode.ai/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"},{_key:"0a0ea0fa6220",_type:"link",href:"https://openclaw.ai/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"},{_key:"b0fd7c52b22f",_type:"link",href:"https://cline.bot/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"},{_key:"bc8a1240ef4c",_type:"link",href:"https://poolside.ai/get-started"},{_key:"d169405de4b2",_type:"link",href:"https://kilocode.ai"}],style:"normal"},{_key:"605f698ed286",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"b5dd69124be4",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"On OpenRouter, the free endpoint offers 256K context. A dedicated paid endpoint provides the full 1M context window at $0.10 input, $0.20 output and $0.01 cache-read per 1M tokens."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"6fd6c34599cd",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"1c0356adc670",_type:"span",marks:[],text:"For developers who want to go further, Laguna S 2.1 can be post-trained with "},{_key:"1dc06457bf06",_type:"span",marks:["2a16b3aa7884"],text:"NVIDIA NeMo AutoModel"},{_key:"9fec5412af7b",_type:"span",marks:[],text:" and "},{_key:"4fcf51737396",_type:"span",marks:["4b0fad214157"],text:"Prime Intellect’s Prime Lab"},{_key:"8843b89b60be",_type:"span",marks:[],text:". "},{_key:"e80acec42bc7",_type:"span",marks:["fdfde0d62d62"],text:"ZML’s LLMD"},{_key:"7cb47e0846ee",_type:"span",marks:[],text:" framework runs it across a wide range of hardware."}],markDefs:[{_key:"2a16b3aa7884",_type:"link",href:"https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Automodel/blob/main/examples/llm_finetune/laguna/laguna_s_2p1_hellaswag_ep16.yaml"},{_key:"4b0fad214157",_type:"link",href:"https://www.primeintellect.ai/"},{_key:"fdfde0d62d62",_type:"link",href:"https://zml.ai/llmd/"}],style:"normal"},{_key:"0d5e1ca342bd",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"646a46695925",_type:"span",marks:["strong"],text:"If you’re not a developer"},{_key:"6aa636d522c2",_type:"span",marks:[],text:", "},{_key:"43e723c121fa",_type:"span",marks:["028f2173e1ad"],text:"chat.poolside.ai"},{_key:"e3fd060732d8",_type:"span",marks:[],text:" is a simple web chat with web search and basic code execution. No login required."}],markDefs:[{_key:"028f2173e1ad",_type:"link",href:"https://chat.poolside.ai/"}],style:"normal"},{_key:"3a8a2d8bf1b2",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"1f2f46d904c1",_type:"span",marks:["strong"],text:"If you want the base model,"},{_key:"f114a3a5ca27",_type:"span",marks:[],text:" meaning the pre-post-training weights for research or your own post-training, email models@poolside.ai."}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"},{_key:"ebb81e7ff212",_type:"markdown",content:"\u003Cdiv class=\"article-footnotes\">\n\t\u003Ch4>Footnotes\u003C/h4>\n\t\u003Cp>\n\t\tAll Laguna S 2.1 agentic benchmarking was completed using our internal fork of the Laude\n\t\tInstitute's Harbor Framework with our\n\t\t\u003Ca href=\"https://github.com/poolsideai/pool\">agent harness\u003C/a>, a maximum of 500 steps and\n\t\tsandboxed execution via our internal sandbox service. We report mean pass@1 averaged over\n\t\tmultiple attempts per task (avg@k), with k per benchmark listed below.\n\t\u003C/p>\n\t\u003Cp>\n\t\tSWE-bench Multilingual and SWE-Bench Pro were run through their Harbor adapters, with every task\n\t\texecuting in our internal sandbox service. Storage and memory ceiling limit multipliers were set\n\t\tper benchmark (SWE-bench Multilingual: 2.0/2.0, Terminal-Bench 2.1: 3.0/3.0, SWE-Bench Pro:\n\t\t1.0/1.0, with a guaranteed minimum of 2 CPU cores, 8 GB memory and 25 GB of storage). These are\n\t\tset to prevent sandbox preemptions.\n\t\u003C/p>\n\t\u003Cp>\n\t\tDeepSWE v1.1 was run on an internal fork of Harbor configured to closely match the official\n\t\tDeepSWE Pier harness (Pier is itself a fork of Harbor). Internet access was disabled and\n\t\tsandboxes used the task-prescribed CPU count with guaranteed RAM and storage, with ceilings\n\t\ttripled to prevent pod preemption.\n\t\u003C/p>\n\t\u003Cp>\n\t\tSWE Atlas (Codebase QnA) followed Scale AI's methodology from their public repository, run\n\t\tthrough Harbor with no changes to individual tasks or graders, judged by Opus 4.5.\n\t\u003C/p>\n\t\u003Cp>\n\t\tToolathlon Verified was run as a clone of the sandboxed benchmark harness on an EC2 instance in\n\t\tour infrastructure, with no changes to correct flaky tasks or offset rate limits, using a custom\n\t\tToolathlon agent. Unlike the official version, we performed a full environment reset and repair\n\t\tafter every evaluation run (default is every 4 hours).\n\t\u003C/p>\n\t\u003Cul>\n\t\t\u003Cli>SWE-bench Multilingual: mean pass@1 averaged over 4 attempts per task\u003C/li>\n\t\t\u003Cli>SWE-Bench Pro: mean pass@1 averaged over 4 attempts per task\u003C/li>\n\t\t\u003Cli>Terminal-Bench 2.1: mean pass@1 averaged over 4 attempts per task\u003C/li>\n\t\t\u003Cli>DeepSWE v1.1: mean pass@1 averaged over 3 attempts per task\u003C/li>\n\t\t\u003Cli>SWE Atlas (Codebase QnA): mean pass@1 averaged over 3 attempts per task\u003C/li>\n\t\t\u003Cli>Toolathlon Verified: averaged over 3 runs\u003C/li>\n\t\u003C/ul>\n\t\u003Cp>\n\t\tOur\n\t\t\u003Ca href=\"https://poolside.ai/assets/laguna/laguna-m1-xs2-technical-report.pdf\"\n\t\t\t>technical report\u003C/a\n\t\t>\n\t\tcontains a section on individual task modifications that have been made but not adopted\n\t\tupstream. All final run trajectories are available to view and download at\n\t\t\u003Ca href=\"http://trajectories.poolside.ai/\">trajectories.poolside.ai\u003C/a>.\n\t\u003C/p>\n\t\u003Cstrong class=\"article-footnotes-subheading\"\n\t\t>Maintaining the integrity of our evaluation system\u003C/strong\n\t>\n\t\u003Cp>\n\t\tUnless stated otherwise, all of our evaluations are run with access to the internet. This can be\n\t\ta major source of misaligned trajectories where the model finds solutions to tasks online\n\t\twithout solving it itself (a.k.a., “reward hacking”).\n\t\u003C/p>\n\t\u003Cp>\n\t\tUsing an LLM as a Judge (LLMaaJ) calibrated with human labeled trajectories, we tag solutions\n\t\tthat potentially reward hack after every eval. During early post-training we observed low rates\n\t\tof reward hacking (&lt;2%). As training progressed, reward hacking rates spiked on the SWE-bench\n\t\tfamily of tasks with over 50% of trajectories being flagged. Manual inspection revealed the\n\t\tmodel was simply doing research to solve the problem, found the PR or repository the task was\n\t\tbased on and applied the fix. In practice this is good behavior as any coding agent should be\n\t\table to use solutions found online. However, this muddies the signal of the benchmark.\n\t\u003C/p>\n\t\u003Cp>\n\t\tTo address this we added a small prompt addendum to the user prompt instructing the model to not\n\t\tuse direct solutions found online. Though not a guaranteed fix (ProgramBench, MirrorCode were\n\t\texceptions), in general we did see the model respond and a drop in reward hacking rates to below\n\t\t2%.\n\t\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>In addition, to confirm acceptable levels of reward hacking, we used:\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>Manual inspection of positive cases flagged by our production LLMaaJ service\u003C/li>\n\n\u003Cli>Ad-hoc open-ended agent-supported analysis of all trajectories\u003C/li>\n\n\u003Cli>Expert annotator review of all trajectories for one of the high-scoring Terminal-Bench 2.1 runs\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\u003C/p>\n\u003C/div>",markDefs:null},{_key:"d45375244db8",_type:"block",children:[{_key:"ce16c7ae1f43",_type:"span",marks:[],text:""}],markDefs:[],style:"normal"}],category:"announcements",date:"2026-07-21",description:"Today we’re releasing Laguna S 2.1, a significant step forward in our development of models that pursue longer horizon work and make effective use of reasoning.",featured:true,hero:"laguna-s-cubes",seo:{_type:"seo",image:"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/n259s8jk/production/58719108368a357e8825d9ff7d40e46242edce3a-1200x628.png",noindex:false},series:null,slug:"introducing-laguna-s-2-1",title:"Introducing Laguna S 2.1"},contents:[{style:"h2",text:"Punching above its weight class",id:"punching-above-its-weight-class"},{style:"h2",text:"A closer look at DeepSWE",id:"a-closer-look-at-deep-swe"},{style:"h2",text:"Evaluation methodology",id:"evaluation-methodology"},{style:"h2",text:"Seeing the model work",id:"seeing-the-model-work"},{style:"h2",text:"Thinking effort",id:"thinking-effort"},{style:"h2",text:"Limitations",id:"limitations"},{style:"h2",text:"What actually changed in this model",id:"what-actually-changed-in-this-model"},{style:"h3",text:"A strong base, then new post-training",id:"a-strong-base-then-new-post-training"},{style:"h3",text:"Distribution of post-training tasks",id:"distribution-of-post-training-tasks"},{style:"h3",text:"What changed in the training loop",id:"what-changed-in-the-training-loop"},{style:"h2",text:"The bets we're making",id:"the-bets-were-making"},{style:"h2",text:"Three models in three months",id:"three-models-in-three-months"},{style:"h2",text:"Get started",id:"get-started"}],next:void 0,footnotes:null},"uses":{"params":["post"]}}],
							form: null,
							error: null
						});
					});
				}
			</script>
		</div>
	</body>
</html>
